---
description: Keep files small — extract named units next to their feature
globs: "{app,components,content,lib}/**/*.{ts,tsx}"
alwaysApply: false
---

# File decomposition

Extract a named unit into its own file when a module gets hard to read. Do not split glue.

## Extract when

- The file is past ~150–200 lines or has 2+ unrelated concerns
- A pure helper, mapper, or formatter has a clear name
- Non-trivial React state belongs in a colocated `use-*.ts`

## Do not extract when

- 5–15 lines used once next to the only caller
- A one-liner that only adds a jump
- “Future reuse” with a single call site

| Kind | Where |
|------|--------|
| UI primitive | `components/ui/` |
| Section or hook | next to the feature |
| Copy, prices, cases | `content/<name>.ts` |
| Shared helper | `lib/<name>.ts` |

```ts
// ❌ BAD — page.tsx owns prices, case art, and the lead form
// ✅ GOOD — content/services.ts + ServiceList.tsx; the page composes them
```

- File name says what it does (`format-price.ts`, not `helpers2.ts`)
- No catch-all `utils.ts`. A second theme in a helper file means split it
